[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
### TL;DR  
In MapLibre GL JS v6 you can no longer resolve a missing sprite icon from inside a `styleimagemissing` handler.  
Instead you register a **missing-style-image resolver** with `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver()`.  
The resolver receives the missing image id, fetches or creates the image, calls `map.addImage(id, image, …)` and returns nothing (its return value is ignored).

Below is a complete, ready-to-copy example that works for both browser-CDN and bundler builds.

---

## 1. Why the old pattern stopped working

```js
// v5 – this used to resolve the request automatically
map.on('styleimagemissing', e => {
  map.addImage(e.id, myGeneratedImage);
});
```

* In v6 `styleimagemissing` is **notify-only** – the event is emitted, but the map does **not** wait for you to add the image.  
* The request stays unresolved, so the layer keeps rendering a transparent placeholder.

The fix is to use the new API introduced in v6:

```js
map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async (id) => {
  // you must add the image yourself; the return value is ignored
  const img = await generateOrFetchImage(id);
  map.addImage(id, img, { sdf: true, pixelRatio: 2 });
});
```

---

## 2. Full example (browser CDN, ESM)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Dynamic missing-icon resolver</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  // 1️⃣ Import the ESM build from the CDN
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  // 2️⃣ Create the map (any style that references an unknown icon, e.g. "my-dynamic-icon")
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        osm: { type: 'raster', tiles: ['https://a.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'], tileSize: 256 }
      },
      layers: [{
        id: 'points',
        type: 'symbol',
        source: 'osm',
        layout: {
          // This icon does NOT exist in the sprite sheet
          'icon-image': 'my-dynamic-icon',
          'icon-size': 1.5
        }
      }]
    },
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2
  });

  // 3️⃣ Register the resolver **before** the map starts loading layers
  map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async (missingId) => {
    // You can generate the image on-the-fly, fetch it from a server,
    // or pull it from an in-memory cache.
    // Here we create a simple red circle with Canvas:
    const size = 64;
    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = canvas.height = size;
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    ctx.fillStyle = 'red';
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(size / 2, size / 2, size / 2 - 2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();

    // Convert canvas → ImageBitmap (preferred for MapLibre)
    const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(canvas);

    // Add the image to the map.  Options are optional; set `sdf:true` if you need
    // signed-distance-field rendering (e.g. for color-tintable icons).
    map.addImage(missingId, bitmap, { sdf: false, pixelRatio: 2 });

    // No need to return anything – the map will automatically re-evaluate the style.
  });

  // 4️⃣ Optional: listen for the old event just for debugging
  map.on('styleimagemissing', e => {
    console.warn('styleimagemissing fired for', e.id);
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What the code does

| Step | Why it matters |
|------|----------------|
| **Import the ESM build** | v6 ships only an ESM bundle (`dist/maplibre-gl.mjs`). Use `type="module"` or a bundler import. |
| **Create the map** | The style references `my-dynamic-icon`, which is not in any sprite. |
| **`setMissingStyleImageResolver`** | Registers a *single* resolver that will be called for **any** missing image id. It can be async, allowing you to fetch from a server or generate on the fly. |
| **`addImage` inside the resolver** | This is the only way to tell the map “here’s the image you asked for”. The map will automatically re-render the layer once the image is added. |
| **`styleimagemissing` listener (optional)** | Still emitted, but only for logging; it does **not** affect resolution. |

---

## 3. Using the resolver in a bundler (Vite, webpack, etc.)

If you’re building with a bundler you still import the same symbols, but you also need to make sure the worker URL is set (see the migration guide). The resolver code itself is identical.

```bash
# Example with Vite
npm i maplibre-gl
```

```js
// src/main.ts
import { Map, setWorkerUrl } from 'maplibre-gl';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';
import workerUrl from 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?worker&url';

// Tell MapLibre where the worker lives (required for bundlers)
setWorkerUrl(workerUrl);

const map = new Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'my-style.json',
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2,
});

// Register the resolver (same as the CDN example)
map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async (id) => {
  const response = await fetch(`/icons/${id}.png`);
  const blob = await response.blob();
  const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(blob);
  map.addImage(id, bitmap);
});
```

> **Note:** The resolver must be registered **before** the map starts loading layers that reference the missing icons. In practice you can call it right after you instantiate `Map`, as shown above.

---

## 4. Common pitfalls & how to avoid them

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **Icon never appears, console shows “styleimagemissing” repeatedly** | You called `map.addImage()` inside a `styleimagemissing` listener (v5 pattern). | Switch to `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver()` (the resolver runs *instead* of the listener). |
| **`addImage` throws “Image already exists”** | The resolver was called twice for the same id (e.g., you added the image manually elsewhere). | Guard against duplicates: `if (!map.hasImage(id)) { map.addImage(...); }` |
| **Image is added but looks garbled** | You passed a raw `<canvas>` element or an `HTMLImageElement` without converting to `ImageBitmap`. | Use `await createImageBitmap(canvasOrImg)` before `addImage`. |
| **Missing icons only on the first load, then work after a refresh** | The resolver was registered *after* the map had already emitted `styleimagemissing`. | Register the resolver **immediately after** creating the `Map`, before any `load` event. |
| **Worker-load error (`Failed to load worker script`)** | Using a bundler without calling `setWorkerUrl()`. | Follow the bundler-specific snippet in the migration guide (Vite: `?worker&url`, webpack/rollup: `new URL('.../maplibre-gl-worker.mjs', import.meta.url)`). |
| **TypeScript error “Cannot find name ‘MapDataEvent’”** | v6 removed `MapDataEvent`. | Use `MapSourceDataEvent | MapStyleDataEvent` instead (not needed for the resolver, but useful if you also listen to `data` events). |

---

## 5. Quick checklist for “dynamic icons at runtime”

1. **Import the ESM build** (`import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'` or via CDN).  
2. **Create the map** (`new maplibregl.Map({ … })`).  
3. **(Bundler only) Call `setWorkerUrl()`** with the worker URL.  
4. **Register a resolver** with `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async id => { … })`.  
5. Inside the resolver:  
   * Fetch/generate the image (Canvas, SVG, PNG, etc.).  
   * Convert to `ImageBitmap` (or `HTMLImageElement` if you prefer).  
   * Call `map.addImage(id, bitmap, { sdf?, pixelRatio? })`.  
6. **Done** – the map will automatically re-draw the layer that requested the icon.

---

## 6. Full TypeScript version (optional)

```ts
import { Map, setWorkerUrl, type MissingStyleImageResolver } from 'maplibre-gl';
import workerUrl from 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?worker&url';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';

setWorkerUrl(workerUrl);

const map = new Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'style.json',
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2,
});

const resolver: MissingStyleImageResolver = async (id) => {
  // Example: fetch a PNG from /icons/<id>.png
  const resp = await fetch(`/icons/${id}.png`);
  if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`Icon ${id} not found`);
  const blob = await resp.blob();
  const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(blob);
  map.addImage(id, bitmap, { sdf: false, pixelRatio: 2 });
};

map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(resolver);
```

---

### TL;DR Recap

* **v5 → v6 change:** `styleimagemissing` no longer resolves the request.  
* **Solution:** `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async id => { …; map.addImage(id, image); })`.  
* Register the resolver **once**, before any layers that might need missing icons are rendered.  
* Works the same in CDN and bundler environments (just remember the bundler-specific `setWorkerUrl()` call).

That’s all you need to supply icons dynamically at runtime in MapLibre GL JS v6! 🚀

Below is the **v6-only** way to supply an icon (or any other image) the moment the style asks for it and can’t find it in the sprite sheet.

---

## 1️⃣ What changed

| v5 (still works in v5) | v6 (the current version) |
|------------------------|--------------------------|
| `map.on('styleimagemissing', …)` → call `map.addImage()` **inside** the handler and the map will automatically use the newly-added image. | `styleimagemissing` is now **notify-only** – calling `addImage()` from the handler does **not** resolve the pending request. |
| No extra API needed. | You must register a **resolver** with `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver()` that returns a `Promise<void>` (or `void`). The resolver is responsible for adding the image itself. |

> **TL;DR** – keep the `styleimagemissing` listener only if you want to be warned, but **use `setMissingStyleImageResolver`** to actually provide the image.

---

## 2️⃣ Minimal working example (ESM)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – dynamic missing icons</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  // 1️⃣ Import the library (CDN ESM build)
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  // 2️⃣ Create the map
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json', // any style that references a missing icon
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2
  });

  // 3️⃣ Register the resolver **once**, before any map is created (or right after creation)
  map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async (missingId) => {
    // `missingId` is the name the style tried to use (e.g. "my-dynamic-pin")
    console.log('Missing image requested:', missingId);

    // ----> YOUR LOGIC TO GET THE image <----
    // You can:
    //   • fetch a PNG/SVG from a server,
    //   • generate a canvas bitmap on the fly,
    //   • use an existing HTMLImageElement, etc.
    // The function must resolve *after* the image has been added to the map.

    // Example: generate a simple 32×32 red circle on a canvas
    const size = 32;
    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = canvas.height = size;
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    ctx.fillStyle = 'red';
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(size / 2, size / 2, size / 2 - 2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();

    // Convert the canvas to an ImageBitmap (preferred for performance)
    const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(canvas);

    // 4️⃣ Add the image to the map – this *must* be called inside the resolver
    map.addImage(missingId, bitmap, { sdf: false, pixelRatio: 2 });

    // No return value is needed; the map will automatically re-evaluate the style
  });

  // Optional: keep the old listener just for debugging / logging
  map.on('styleimagemissing', (e) => {
    console.warn('styleimagemissing event (notify-only):', e.id);
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What the code does

1. **Imports the ESM build** (`dist/maplibre-gl.mjs`).  
   *If you’re using a bundler, import from `'maplibre-gl'` instead and remember the `setWorkerUrl()` step (see the migration guide).*

2. **Creates the map** with any style that references an image that isn’t in the sprite sheet.

3. **Registers a resolver** with `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver`.  
   The resolver receives the missing image’s **id** (`e.id` from the old `styleimagemissing` event).  
   Inside the resolver you:
   * fetch or generate the image,
   * optionally convert it to an `ImageBitmap` (or keep it as an `HTMLImageElement`/`ImageData`),
   * call `map.addImage(id, image, options)`.

4. The map automatically re-renders the layer that requested the image once `addImage` resolves.

---

## 3️⃣ Common patterns for the resolver

### 3.1 Fetch a PNG/SVG from a remote URL

```js
map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async (id) => {
  const response = await fetch(`https://my.cdn.com/icons/${id}.png`);
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Icon ${id} not found`);
  const blob = await response.blob();
  const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(blob);
  map.addImage(id, bitmap);
});
```

### 3.2 Generate an SVG on the fly

```js
function svgToBitmap(svgString) {
  const blob = new Blob([svgString], { type: 'image/svg+xml' });
  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const img = new Image();
    img.onload = async () => {
      const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(img);
      URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
      resolve(bitmap);
    };
    img.onerror = (e) => reject(e);
    img.src = url;
  });
}

map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async (id) => {
  const svg = `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32">
                 <text x="50%" y="50%" dominant-baseline="middle" text-anchor="middle"
                       font-size="20" fill="white">${id[0].toUpperCase()}</text>
               </svg>`;
  const bitmap = await svgToBitmap(svg);
  map.addImage(id, bitmap);
});
```

### 3.3 Use a pre-loaded `HTMLImageElement`

```js
const preloaded = new Image();
preloaded.src = '/assets/default-pin.png';
preloaded.onload = () => {
  map.setMissingStyleImageResolver((id) => {
    // reuse the same image for every missing id
    map.addImage(id, preloaded);
  });
};
```

> **Tip:** If you need different images per id, keep a `Map<string, HTMLImageElement>` cache and look them up inside the resolver.

---

## 4️⃣ TypeScript typings (v6)

```ts
import type {
  Map,
  MissingStyleImageResolver,
  StyleImageMissingEvent
} from 'maplibre-gl';

declare const map: Map;

// The resolver type is `(id: string) => void | Promise<void>`
const resolver: MissingStyleImageResolver = async (id) => {
  // …your async logic…
  map.addImage(id, await fetchBitmap(id));
};

map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(resolver);

// If you still want the notification event (optional)
map.on('styleimagemissing', (e: StyleImageMissingEvent) => {
  console.log('Missing image requested (notify-only):', e.id);
});
```

*`MissingStyleImageResolver` and `StyleImageMissingEvent` are exported from `maplibre-gl` starting with v6.*

---

## 5️⃣ Gotchas & FAQs

| Issue | Why it happens | Fix |
|-------|----------------|-----|
| **The map stays blank after a missing-icon request** | You called `map.addImage()` from a `styleimagemissing` listener (v5 pattern). In v6 that does **not** resolve the request. | Switch to `setMissingStyleImageResolver` (as shown above). |
| **`addImage` throws “Image already exists”** | The resolver was called twice for the same id (e.g., the style re-requests while the first async fetch is still pending). | Cache the promise or the bitmap yourself, or guard with `if (!map.hasImage(id)) …`. |
| **The resolver never runs** | You’re using a bundler that loads the **UMD** build (`dist/maplibre-gl.js`). v6 no longer ships a UMD bundle, so the import fails silently and the map never starts. | Use the ESM build (`dist/maplibre-gl.mjs`) or import from the package entry (`import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'`). |
| **Worker-loading errors in a bundler** | Bundlers don’t automatically resolve the worker URL. | Call `setWorkerUrl()` once (see migration guide) **before** creating the `Map`. |
| **I need the raw projection matrix** | `map.transform` was removed; the matrix is only available inside a custom layer’s `render` callback. | Use the public camera getters (`getZoom()`, `getCenter()`, …) or, inside a custom layer, read `projectionData` from the `render` arguments. |
| **I’m still on CommonJS (`require`)** | v6 exports only an `"import"` entry; `require('maplibre-gl')` throws `ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED`. | Convert the file to ESM (`import … from 'maplibre-gl'`) or load dynamically: `const { Map } = await import('maplibre-gl');`. |

---

## 6️⃣ Quick checklist for a **working dynamic-icon setup** in v6

1. **Import the ESM build** (`dist/maplibre-gl.mjs` or `import … from 'maplibre-gl'` in a bundler).  
2. **Create the map** (or wait for `style.load` if you need the style first).  
3. **Call `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(...)`** *once* (before any missing-icon request can happen).  
4. Inside the resolver:  
   * fetch / generate the image,  
   * optionally convert to `ImageBitmap` (recommended),  
   * call `map.addImage(id, image, options)`.  
5. (Optional) Keep a `styleimagemissing` listener only for logging.  
6. If you’re using a bundler, **don’t forget** the `setWorkerUrl()` call (different per bundler).  

---

### TL;DR code snippet (ESM, minimal)

```js
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';

const map = new maplibregl.Map({ container: 'map', style: 'style.json' });

map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async (id) => {
  const resp = await fetch(`/icons/${id}.png`);
  const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(await resp.blob());
  map.addImage(id, bitmap);
});
```

That’s all you need to **dynamically supply missing icons at runtime** in MapLibre GL JS v6. Happy mapping!

