## 1️⃣ Install the library (and its CSS)

```bash
npm i maplibre-gl@^6
# optional – if you want the default sprite/font assets locally:
npm i -D copy-webpack-plugin   # (or any copy tool you already use)
```

> **Pin the major version** (`@^6`) so a future major bump won’t silently break the app.

---

## 2️⃣ Vite config (only if you want to tweak the worker handling)

Vite’s default ESM handling works out-of-the-box, but you may want to make sure the worker file is emitted as a separate asset. The simplest way is to rely on Vite’s built-in `?worker&url` query (no extra config needed).

```ts
// vite.config.ts (optional – only if you have custom asset handling)
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';   // or your framework plugin

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  // No special worker config required – Vite will treat "?worker&url" as an asset URL.
